{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers","id":1353517,"title":"Reverse Engineering the Prometheus chambers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-08T03:13:37-08:00","id":1353517,"title":"Reverse Engineering the Prometheus chambers","content":"So as a thought, especially once the Doyen are revealed as not so nice, it's likely that the Prometheus chambers are going to become a big issue, if for no other reason than nobody knows whether or not there's a self-destruct somewhere in there.<br /> <br /> So, as an objective for a campaign, how hard would it e to reverse engineer a Prometheus chamber? Let's assume three cases:<br /> <br /> 1. You're using psions, talents and superiors only as your researchers.<br /> <br /> 2. You've managed to convince/find some megaintelligent novas who are willing to add their smarts (keep in mind that they can't directly percieve noetic energies, which is going to make them less helpful than they might otherwise be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, presuming you could reverse engineer them, what would a prometheus chamber with no limitations look like? My general assumption is that such a design would get you a psiad, since the psions aren't simply limited--they're rather boosted. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T04:16:15-08:00","id":1353523,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, Novas <i>can't</i> develop noetic biotech. Talents are limited at best because they can't use/develop &quot;powered&quot; items. So, you're pretty much stuck with psions and psiads.<br /> <br /> For my part it'd be something that would take years if not decades to do. <br /> <br /> The main thing to consider is that the chambers aren't really adding anything to the humans in them as such, they're maximizing and reworking what's already there.<br /> <br /> Say you have a man who is 6 feet tall and weighs 200 pounds. If you somehow reshaped him into somebody who was 12 feet tall, he'd still be 200 pounds but he'd be really thin and spindly because his overall mass hasn't changed.<br /> <br /> The Prometheus chambers don't change people's psionic &quot;mass.&quot; They shape and focus it in a particular direction. A psion can reach 5 dots in his Aptitude and 1 dot in any other Aptitude mode. One who transcends to Psi 6 or 7 can reach 6 or 7 in his Aptitude and up to 2 dots in other modes.<br /> <br /> By contrast a Psiad can only get to 3 dots in any mode unless they transcend (or take the Strong Mode edge which lets them reach 4 dots in a single mode). One who transcends up to 6 Psi can reach 4 dots in his primary modes (Quantakinesis and two others) but is still limited to 3 dots in Secondary Aptitudes. Again, Strong Mode will let them raise one of their Primary Modes to 5 dots or one secondary Mode to 4 dots.<br /> <br /> Is it possible that a decade or so of work by Psi-empowered supergeniuses could create Chambers that endow Super-Psiad that have the flexibility of Psiads with the power level of Psions? Sure. But it's beyond the scope of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:26:09-08:00","id":1353615,"title":"","content":"Nova geniuses did cure a huge number of genetically based illnesses and used bioengineered substances to fight global pollution, so a suitably focused Nova should be able to analyze the genetic component of the device. An understanding of the brain may even let them uncover any booby traps that were probably installed to make Psions easier to manipulate via Telepathy. Anything beyond straightforward copy/paste alterations would likely be much, much harder to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T14:03:45-08:00","id":1353631,"title":"","content":"As I recall the original plan for the 1e Africa book Bright Continent was to have a new &quot;order&quot; show up that had built new promenthius chambers (I forget which ones) after studying parts of the QK chamber. I seem to recall that this was also intended to lead to a 2e where the order divisions were much blurrier (I suspect in much the way they are in the actual 2e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T14:10:57-08:00","id":1353632,"title":"","content":"This seems like a project for the Chitra banu. <br /> They have the chamber, the motivation and a proxy able to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T16:00:00-08:00","id":1353645,"title":"","content":"I honestly would have much preferred one generic Prometheus Chamber tech which in-setting picks a random Aptitude to empower when someone goes through it. (Out of game there is no randomness to it, the player gets to choose, even though the character didn't.) <br /> <br /> Actually, honestly, nothing says this still can't happen. The Orders discover what the Doyn are doing and so they and Aeon get together to break down the whole &quot;each chamber unlocks only one type) when they build the Doyn-free second edition of the Prometheus Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T04:27:36-08:00","id":1353759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353523#post1353523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible that a decade or so of work by Psi-empowered supergeniuses could create Chambers that endow Super-Psiad that have the flexibility of Psiads with the power level of Psions? Sure. But it's beyond the scope of this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my memory is right, one of the side effects of the Venezuela Phenomena was the random increase in Psi user\u2019s power levels.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t believe they ever released rules for it, but it does show that there are ways for devices that can be made in the Trinity setting (Hammersmith devices in this instance) to boost Psi users to new levels of potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353631#post1353631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall the original plan for the 1e Africa book Bright Continent was to have a new &quot;order&quot; show up that had built new promenthius chambers (I forget which ones) after studying parts of the QK chamber. I seem to recall that this was also intended to lead to a 2e where the order divisions were much blurrier (I suspect in much the way they are in the actual 2e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I vaguely recall something about this. Was this shared by Bruce Baugh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T05:13:58-08:00","id":1353767,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s impossible for a Nova to reverse engineering Prometheus chamber, but for sure a team of EKs and VKs can try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T08:05:10-08:00","id":1353843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vjornin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353632#post1353632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a project for the Chitra banu.<br /> They have the chamber, the motivation and a proxy able to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have an advantage in that their proxy had experience making advanced noetic tech well before the creation of the Psi Orders, since she was the one responsible for the device which caused the global noetic surge that lead to the Doyen creating the Prometheus Chambers. I believe she also lead the project to repair their chamber after the destruction of their headquarters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353767#post1353767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019s impossible for a Nova to reverse engineering Prometheus chamber, but for sure a team of EKs and VKs can try.</div> </div> </div> </div>While they can certainly try, I figure the Doyen (being completely paranoid) specifically designed the chambers to be as close to impossible for psions to reverse engineer as possible. Even with Novas being incapable of making proper noetic biotech, their alternate approach to advanced devices could let them make more progress than psions. This is helped by the way that high Mega-Intellect Novas with the proper edges are flat out smarter than an Intellect 7 (through Vitakinesis) psion inventor can even imagine. Of course I think the Psi Orders would then want to reverse engineer the Nova version in order to make a proper device that operates on purely noetic technology.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, no one is likely to willingly let a Nova near a Prometheus Chamber, and the Doyen could have designed the Prometheus Chambers to self destruct if a Nova ever gets too close (although that'd have to be pretty close, since the quantakinetics were apparently studying Novas and sub-aberrants at their headquarters facility), so that'd make it virtually impossible for them to make progress in any way that doesn't involve remote inspection via advanced sensors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T09:10:33-08:00","id":1353861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353759#post1353759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If my memory is right, one of the side effects of the Venezuela Phenomena was the random increase in Psi user\u2019s power levels.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t believe they ever released rules for it, but it does show that there are ways for devices that can be made in the Trinity setting (Hammersmith devices in this instance) to boost Psi users to new levels of potential.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly true, but this is still a game and the Psions=deep; Psiads=Broad is a way to maintain game balance and also to make sure that players of Psions don't think they screwed up by not playing Psiads. Still, your game, your rules. If you decide you want Talented Psi-Novas, have a nut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353759#post1353759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I vaguely recall something about this. Was this shared by Bruce Baugh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard anything about that. Any details/sources?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:00:59-08:00","id":1353902,"title":"","content":"To be honest I don't remember exactly where I heard that. I think it was something Baugh posted, in the same post where he talked about wanting Mercer to roll up in front of Aeon era Trinity in 20's roadster with a Daredevil Qin. But, it was a long time ago now so I could be misremebering some details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:02:39-08:00","id":1353920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353759#post1353759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I vaguely recall something about this. Was this shared by Bruce Baugh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno if Bruce ever shared it, but Ian Watson did. Bruce planned the new order for Bright Continent, Ian decided they needed a Chamber to make them a full order. Have a look through Ian's posts in <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/trinity-ians-plans.596494/\" target=\"_blank\">this RPGnet thread</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 12-09-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:55:24-08:00","id":1353931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353920#post1353920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno if Bruce ever shared it, but Ian Watson did. Bruce planned the new order for Bright Continent, Ian decided they needed a Chamber to make them a full order. Have a look through Ian's posts in <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/trinity-ians-plans.596494/\" target=\"_blank\">this RPGnet thread</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, that takes me back. It was about a month before Rich approached me to see if I'd be interested in the project that eventually became the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:28:23-08:00","id":1353977,"title":"","content":"Noetic tech, the same way as quantum tech, is more than just what we see. There is a noetic pattern/lattice (what ever they call) that goes beyond the material and make it work as it works (in the case o quantum tech a quantum lattice). The other template can\u2019t reach that pattern and so can\u2019t make it work or even reverse engineering it.<br /> <br /> The only thing a nova can do is boost a psion/psiad to make them more capable...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T23:41:22-08:00","id":1354076,"title":"","content":"With the official exception of QK, of course. I'm guessing that a sufficiently skilled quantakinetic engineer could probably grok Novatech. Not as well as a comparable Nova engineer could, mind you; but my take on it is that the difference is more a matter of how much experience is needed and hope reliable the effort is than a blanket \u201cA can do it, but B can't\u201d. <br /> <br /> If there's a Quantum counterpart to QK (e.g., a Quantum Power that specializes in manipulation of psychic energies), I'd expect that to work the other way: such a Nova could puzzle out noetic technology, just not as easily as a psion can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T01:09:48-08:00","id":1354087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1354076#post1354076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's a Quantum counterpart to QK (e.g., a Quantum Power that specializes in manipulation of psychic energies), I'd expect that to work the other way: such a Nova could puzzle out noetic technology, just not as easily as a psion can.</div> </div> </div> </div>There explicitly isn\u2019t. Psi can have limited influence on quantum, quantum can\u2019t do the same to psi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T02:38:42-08:00","id":1354095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1353977#post1353977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noetic tech, the same way as quantum tech, is more than just what we see. There is a noetic pattern/lattice (what ever they call) that goes beyond the material and make it work as it works (in the case o quantum tech a quantum lattice). The other template can\u2019t reach that pattern and so can\u2019t make it work or even reverse engineering it.<br /> <br /> The only thing a nova can do is boost a psion/psiad to make them more capable...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say that is entirely true. A nova, especially a super genius one, say the ones who max out their mega int, may not be able to <i>directly</i> work with the tech--but when ws that last time you saw a nuclear engineer or theorist directly work with protons or exotic particles? Being able to work with psions and normals to work on the theory of what is happening could get those who do hav ethe ability to directly work with things like noetic technology the information they need to make the modification.<br /> <br /> It also would play into the Unity them of course--all branches of mankind doing together what they could not do alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T09:02:18-08:00","id":1354172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1354095#post1354095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that is entirely true. A nova, especially a super genius one, say the ones who max out their mega int, may not be able to <i>directly</i> work with the tech--but when ws that last time you saw a nuclear engineer or theorist directly work with protons or exotic particles? Being able to work with psions and normals to work on the theory of what is happening could get those who do hav ethe ability to directly work with things like noetic technology the information they need to make the modification.<br /> <br /> It also would play into the Unity them of course--all branches of mankind doing together what they could not do alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mega-Intelligent Nova could potentially develop an extremely sophisticated theoretical understanding of Neotics. But they couldn't do anything concrete with it. They couldn't build a Noetic device. If a Noetic super-scientist came up with some, the Nova could probably &quot;check the math&quot; but that's pretty much it.<br /> <br /> The same general thing is true of Psions/Psiads - including Quantakinetics. QKs can manipulate Quantum forces but only directly in specific ways (Energetics/Transmutation). They can also indirectly manipulation Quantum in relatively crude ways (Drain/Transferance). None of that would be sufficient to allow them to develop or even use Q-tech. They might be able to manipulate the environment or boost an aspect of Q-tech with their powers, but that's it.<br /> <br /> Theoretically a Nova could potentially do something similar (Absorption or Quantum Leech with an &quot;Affects Psi (2)&quot; tag). Maybe Boost with &quot;Affects Psi&quot; (2), Bestow Only(0)). Presumably powers like this would be at increased Difficulty and/or spend their success on a 2 for 1 basis (leeches/boosts 1 Psi for every 2-4 successes). Ultimately though, if you want to use Psi, play a Psion/Psiad. If you want Quantum, play a Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T09:07:21-08:00","id":1354175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1354172#post1354172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Mega-Intelligent Nova could potentially develop an extremely sophisticated theoretical understanding of Neotics. But they couldn't do anything concrete with it. They couldn't build a Noetic device. If a Noetic super-scientist came up with some, the Nova could probably &quot;check the math&quot; but that's pretty much it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with that, and I would say that would allow them to use the teamwork rules to assist the psion(s) trying to recreate the chambers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T10:49:52-08:00","id":1354206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1353517-reverse-engineering-the-prometheus-chambers?p=1354175#post1354175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would agree with that, and I would say that would allow them to use the teamwork rules to assist the psion(s) trying to recreate the chambers.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my part I'd want to place limits on what could be done with the Chambers. I might do stuff like:<br /> <br /> Doyen &quot;malware&quot; removed so that any Enhancements against Psions the Doyen would receive due to &quot;backdoors&quot; and other things that were built into the chambers would be eliminated. I would otherwise give the Doyen a minimum +2 Enhancement for using their powers against Psions (but not Psiads).<br /> <br /> Psions/Psiads getting dunked &quot;redunked&quot; may choose to remove/repurpose a Dot from one of their Favored Approach Attributes (or apply the bonus Dot the Chamber would give them) and apply it to Psi instead (to a maximum of 5). So a Psions could potentially start with a Psi of 4 instead of 3.<br /> <br /> Psions/Psiads may become &quot;Psi-optimized.&quot; They pay 1 XP less for any Psi-related improvements/additions (Psi, Modes/AuxiliaryModes, Psi-related Edges like Enhanced Attunement, etc.). Thus new Psi points 5 or below would cost 11 XP instead of 10, a Psi-related Path Edge like Enhanced Attunement would only cost 1 XP, even a Noetic Artifact would cost less. This focus comes with the cost that non-Psi XP purchases cost 1 XP more. So, new/additional Skill dots would cost 6 XP instead of 5. This would instead be defined as an Enhanced Edge (Preq. Minimum Psi 3, Psion or Psiad with a Psi Order Society Path) that's available now that incorporates its own bonus at time of purchase, so it would cost 5 XP instead of 6 XP.<br /> <br /> Psions could gain a New Edge called Strong Auxiliary Mode (3 dots), which gives them all the advantages of Favored Mode and also allows them to buy one additional Dot in that Mode (2 dots at Tier II, 3 Dots at Tier III). A Psion may not have this Edge and Favored Mode. However, if they already have Favored Mode in an Auxiliary Mode they may buy an addition Edge Dot and &quot;upgrade&quot; the Favored Mode to a Strong Auxiliary Mode.<br /> <br /> Not to be left out, Psiads could buy an Enhanced Edge called Augmented Mode (Preq. Favored Aptitude in a Primary Aptitude, Strong Mode within the same Primary Aptitude, Psi 5+): A Psiad with this Enhanced Edge may raise all his Modes within this one Aptitude by one dot further than normal. So, a Psiad with Psi 5 could raise his dots in one chosen Primary Aptitude to 4 dots instead of topping out at three. A Psiad reaching Psi 6, could thus raise his Mode up to 5 in that Aptitude. This supercedes the Strong Mode effect. A Psiad cannot take this Edge in, say, Vitakinesis with a Strong Mode in Latrosis, to be able to Raise Latrosis to 5 at Psi 5 and then to 6 at Psi 6. A lucky, dedicated few Psiads can potentially touch the limits available to Psions, but their genetic nature keeps the powers of the Proxy Tier Psions closed to them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}